{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneStandardRepQDim","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneStandardRepQDim","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.wedderburn_trace_identity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_standard_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_standard_hook","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneStandardRepQDim.lean#L60-L79","doc":"**The standard-representation q-dimension identity, for all `n ≥ 2`**\n(multiplicative form, division-free):\n\n  `[n]_q!  =  [n−1]_q · ([n]_q · [n−2]_q! · [1]_q)`,\n\nwhere the parenthesized factor is the hook-length product of the two-row\nhook shape `λ = (n−1, 1)` — hooks `{n} ∪ {n−2, …, 1}` in row 0, `{1}` in\nrow 1.  Equivalently `d_q(n−1, 1) = [n]_q! / ∏hooks = [n−1]_q`.\n\nThis **generalizes `shape_41`** (the `n = 5` case `d_q(4,1) = [4]_q`) to the\nwhole standard-representation family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_succ","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneStandardRepQDim.lean#L55-L58","doc":"**q-factorial recursion** `[n+1]_q! = [n]_q! · [n+1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qIntGeo_one'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qIntGeo_one'","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneStandardRepQDim.lean#L51-L53","doc":"`[1]_q = 1` (the unbalanced q-integer `[k]_q = ∑_{i<k} q^i`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}